  "question": {
    "text": "If the origin and the non-real roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∀</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></math> are the vertices of an equilateral triangle in the argand plane, then <math><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> times the length of the triangle is",
